course: dictionary
lesson: 7871
title: Rainwater
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Rainwater is water that has fallen from the sky as rain. The word is made of two smaller words, rain and water, so you can often work out a new word by splitting it into parts. Read the context: «Rainwater is slightly acidic and slowly dissolves rocks such as limestone.» The sentence is about water that falls from the sky, and it can wear rock away slowly.
explain: Rainwater is part of the water cycle. Water evaporates, forms clouds, falls as rain and runs into rivers and the sea, and then the cycle starts again. «Some rainwater soaks into the ground and becomes groundwater, which feeds wells and springs.» So rain does not only flow into rivers. Some of it sinks into the soil.
explain: People often collect rainwater in a water butt or a rainwater tank, then use it to water their gardens. This saves tap water. Do not drink rainwater straight from the sky or from drains, because it is not safe unless it has been treated, and drain and flood water can be dirty and dangerous.
explain: Animals and plants use rainwater too. «Bromeliads grow on branches and catch rainwater in a cup of leaves, a tiny pond for insects.» Always check a meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does "water that has fallen as rain" still make sense there? Yes, so you have understood it.
fact: Rainwater means water that has fallen as rain.
fact: Rainwater has no plural, so we never say rainwaters.
fact: «Collect rainwater» and «rainwater butt» are useful phrases to remember.
fact: Rainwater is not safe to drink unless it has been treated.
fact: Some rainwater soaks into the ground and becomes groundwater.
exercise: What is rainwater? | Water that comes out of a tap in a house | Water made by plants in the soil | Water that is always salty like the sea | *Water that has fallen as rain
exercise: «Some rainwater soaks into the ground and becomes groundwater.» Where does this rainwater go? | Into a tap in the kitchen | Into a water butt that is always full | *Into the ground | Straight up into the sky as sunlight
exercise: Why do people use a water butt? | To make fizzy drinks | *To collect rainwater for watering gardens | To store cold tap water for the fridge | To make the sea less salty
test: Rainwater is not always safe to drink. Why? | *It is not safe unless it has been treated | It has no minerals at all | It is always sweet and clean | It is always too hot to touch
test: «A pet flytrap needs rainwater instead of tap water.» Why is rainwater better for it? | Rainwater makes flytraps grow in winter | Tap water is too cold for plants | Rainwater is full of burger | *Tap water has minerals that slowly harm it
exam: Which phrase from the lesson names a container that people use to catch rainwater? | Water cycle | *Rainwater tank | Acidic rock | Groundwater well
